# Agent-created git worktrees. Each is a FULL second copy of the tree, so any gate
# that walks the filesystem with Path.rglob (which descends into dot-directories,
# unlike glob.glob) scans it too. In 2026-08 a stray worktree doubled the corpus for
# three gates and silently defeated zh-hans-localize.py's PROTECT allowlist, whose
# repo-relative paths never match a worktree copy. Previously only in this machine's
# .git/info/exclude; tracked here so every contributor gets the same protection.
.claude/worktrees/
